Z||000000||flexableface||09-21-2000||05:54 PM||||i was wondering what the difference between a 2.8 v-6 and a 2.8 HO engine, if there is any differnce at all. Or is there even such thing as a 2.8 HO???? thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2000||06:21 PM||||Yes there is such a thing as a 2.8 HO.<BR>It can be found in Cameros and Firebirds. Unfortunatly they can't be used in a Fiero due to block differences. The difference is in the top face of the pistons and they can be used in the Fiero by changing them out to increase you Compression Ratio. Bore and stroke in these engines are the same as well as all the bearing journals.||||reg||1
Z||000002||flexableface||09-21-2000||06:43 PM||||thanks for the info||||reg||1
